[agent:result]     TESTBED_COMPUTE_DENY, TESTBED_PLATFORM.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Contract: everything runs on the platform, nothing locally. Bash execs are a
[agent:result]     FAIL-CLOSED allowlist — only the mode's own interface plus basic shell;
[agent:result]     node/ruby/perl/curl/any other binary denied by default:
[agent:result]       - CLI mode → only the platform CLI; NO local python, NO other interpreters.
[agent:result]       - MCP mode → only MCP tools; NO local python/interpreters, NO platform CLI.
[agent:result]       - SDK mode → only the platform SDK's python; NO ML libraries, NO other
[agent:result]         interpreters, NO platform CLI, NO MCP.
[agent:result]       - ML libraries blocked locally in EVERY mode.
[agent:result]     Basic shell (cp/mkdir/ls/cat/grep …) stays allowed to write the floor
[agent:result]     submission and inspect data.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     `segments` may carry the pre-parsed `_pipeline_segments(command)` so the
[agent:result]     caller can reuse one parse across checks; None → parse here.
[agent:result]     """
